  "authored_scope": "Random scenes: an 8-connected two-wall strip running between opposite grid edges. The walls are random walks with steps of up to 3, and the strip width varies by row. Horizontal or diagonal stick-colour rungs join the walls and cut the strip into pockets. Scenes also have wall-attached spurs, isolated loose dots inside the strip, and isolated 1-4 cell distractor sticks of either colour outside. A random transpose and flips set the orientation. Grid sides are in 14..30, and about 40% of sampled sides are 30. Sizes other than 30x30 are synthetic extensions. The three colours are distinct and drawn from 0..9; partially specified colours are honoured. Not supported: strips that bend from one edge to an adjacent edge (seen in three of the four fixtures), closed outlines that do not touch the grid edge, and hand-drawn irregular outlines. Original fixtures are replayed through input_grid with a local flood fill. Their outlines have no compact latent parameterisation, so this replay is used only by validate().",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "bg, wall and stick colours are pairwise distinct; explicit duplicates raise ValueError",
    "each wall run stays within columns 1..w-2, so both outside regions are single 4-connected regions through the grid border columns",
    "inside width per row is 2..10, and consecutive wall runs are 8-connected so no outside cell is 4-adjacent to an inside cell",
    "both outside areas exceed the total inside area by more than 4, so the two outside regions are strictly the two largest regions",
    "at least one rung joins the two walls into one 8-connected wall component",
    "the total count of stick cells joined to the wall is at most wall cells - 3, so the wall colour is the strict majority of the wall component",
    "loose dots and outside distractors are 8-isolated from all other non-background cells, so the wall component stays strictly largest",
    "rung and spur rows are separated by busy-row bookkeeping, so they never touch",
    "every scene has at least one inside background cell, so the output is never the identity",
    "explicit width/height outside 14..30 raise ValueError; input_grid cannot be combined with scene parameters",
    "all retry loops are bounded (60 size/orientation attempts x 400 geometry attempts)"
  ],
